gXD(){return"Sync (if you turn it on): everything is encrypted on your device before it leaves. The Mirinu relay only stores unreadable blocks, with no account and no email address; nobody, not even us, can read them. Without sync, nothing from your library leaves your device."},
gXA(){return"The app contacts metadata services (TMDB through the Mirinu relay, MangaUpdates, MangaDex) to fetch posters, synopses and release dates: these requests contain the title you searched for, nothing else. No ads, no trackers, no analytics."},
gXx(){return"ID matching: to recognize the titles of a MyAnimeList import, the app asks the Mirinu relay which entry matches each MyAnimeList number in the file (only those numbers, nothing else from the file). When you pick or confirm an entry during an import, it also sends the pair of numbers (for example \u201cMyAnimeList 16498 = TMDB 1429\u201d), in a batch, a few seconds later, or at the next launch if you were offline. Each pair comes with a fingerprint computed on your device from a random number that never leaves it: the fingerprint changes from one title to the next, so two pairs sent by the same device cannot be linked to each other. No account, no device ID, no title, no rating, nothing else from your library. Your IP address is not kept: the relay only keeps a 4-character value, mixed with a secret and specific to each pair, used only to count distinct networks. Why: a pair confirmed by several devices is checked by hand by the Mirinu team; if it is correct, it helps other users' imports find the right entry on the first try. No pair sent is used before that check. To stop: Settings, \u201cHelp improve matching\u201d (on by default); turning it off also deletes the pending pairs and the random number. What has already been sent can no longer be linked to you, so it can't be found or deleted at your request."},
gXw(){return"Backups (automatic ones and exports) are local files under your control. Clearing the app's data or uninstalling it deletes everything."},
gXy(){return"Imports (TV Time, Trakt, MyAnimeList, Letterboxd, Netflix) read an export file that you provide yourself; that file is never sent anywhere."},
